{"ok":true,"canonical_id":"AUTOSAR/CP/record/SWS_EthTSyn_00160","versions":[{"version_id":"AUTOSAR/CP/record/SWS_EthTSyn_00160@rel:R19-11#0779df7f","canonical_id":"AUTOSAR/CP/record/SWS_EthTSyn_00160","release":"R19-11","content":"On invocation of EthTSyn_RxIndication() the ingress timestamp t2 shall be retrieved from the EthIf via EthIf_GetIngressTimeStamp() on ingress of the Pdelay_Req message according to Figure 8 , if EthTSynHardwareTimestampSupport ( ECUC_EthTSyn_00018 : ) is set to TRUE . If the StbM does not use the Ethernet controller as source for the Virtual Local Time (refer to parameter StbMLocalTimeHardware , ECUC _StbM_00053 , in [4] ), the EthTSyn shall convert the ingress time stamp to the Virtual Local Time as used in the StbM.","meta":{"trigger_kind":"multi_release_ingest","source_pdf":"AUTOSAR_SWS_TimeSyncOverEthernet.pdf"},"recorded_at":"2026-10-01T10:12:23+00:00","cleaning":{"rule":"spec-text-clean@1","raw_sha256":"0779df7f00aa57075e7ab6b13eab72d8281e0f4d9711d7bce4f2af68056c6ed8","removed":["Specification of Time Synchronization over Ethernet AUTOSAR CP R19 - 11 22 of 83 Document ID 676 : AUTOSAR_SWS_TimeSyncOverEthernet - AUTOSAR confidential -"]},"text_key":"f5162f030547"},{"version_id":"AUTOSAR/CP/record/SWS_EthTSyn_00160@rel:R20-11#b3ceb292","canonical_id":"AUTOSAR/CP/record/SWS_EthTSyn_00160","release":"R20-11","content":"On invocation of EthTSyn_RxIndication() the ingress timestamp t2 shall be retrieved from the EthIf via EthI f_GetIngressTimeStamp() on ingress of the Pdelay_Req message according to Figure 7 , if EthTSynHardwareTimestampSupport ( ECUC_EthTSyn_00018 : ) is set to TRUE . If the StbM does not use the Etherne t controller as source for the Virtual Local Time (refer to parameter StbMLocalTimeHardware , ECUC_StbM_00053 , in [4] ), the EthTSyn shall convert the ingress time stamp to the Virtual Local Time as used in the StbM.","meta":{"trigger_kind":"multi_release_ingest","source_pdf":"AUTOSAR_SWS_TimeSyncOverEthernet.pdf"},"reco